From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:13:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-124: the properties grid's Reset with several
 selected = each one back to its own .dfm value; a double click on True /
 False switches once (0.124.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From the manuals check (EastSun 20261001 "網路上手冊…結果跟網路上不一樣"):
- Reset on a row with several selected wrote the PRIMARY one's .dfm value into all of them (Label2's
  Left 50 became Label1's 10) -- a silent wrong value. Now the panel sends resetProp and the extension
  takes cmdResetToDfm's path (each one's own .dfm value, through lookAll / dfmdiff) for that one
  property only, ONE edit; a row whose values differ can be reset too. (VS Properties window
  "Reset"; C++Builder Object Inspector: a shared property's change goes to all selected.)
- A double click on a True / False value (Visible, Enabled, Font.Bold, AutoSize, IO Value...) was two
  switches (back where it was, two undo steps): the second click is dropped, and a double click on the
  value's empty part switches it once -- the Object Inspector's "toggle their settings by
  double-clicking in the Value column".
Tests: panels (2 selected: Left's Reset = resetProp:Left; double click on Bold = one setLook, on the
box and on the cell); smoke (resetProp Font.Bold = only bold, the move left alone). run_all 3/3
layers (lib 168, smoke 198).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
